New skeleton family error registry (v1.0.0), no codes allocated yet\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Utility\",\n      \"TS\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Utility_bejson_errors.ts\",\n      \"2026-07-18\",\n      \"New skeleton family error registry (v1.0.0), no codes allocated yet\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/data/metadata.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-18\",\n      \"Redesigned as EAV-style (RECORD_TYPE/KEY/VALUE) to hold both per-family versions AND governance rules (Core language-parity requirement, MFDB-is-part-of-Core), per Elton's clarification\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_bejson_core.py\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"v2.0.4: added BEJSON acronym clarification (BOEHNEN ELTON JSON) to header per Elton's direct order\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"JS\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_bejson_core.js\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"v2.0.4: added BEJSON acronym clarification (BOEHNEN ELTON JSON) to header per Elton's direct order\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"TS\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_bejson_core.ts\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"v2.1.2: added BEJSON acronym clarification (BOEHNEN ELTON JSON) to header per Elton's direct order\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"SH\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_bejson_core.sh\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"v2.0.4: added BEJSON acronym clarification (BOEHNEN ELTON JSON) to header per Elton's direct order\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"System\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"lib_bejson_System_be_pms.py\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"Deprecated and moved to Lib_PY/System/Deprecated/. Project management system being rebuilt from scratch; do not use.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"System\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"lib_bejson_System_be_project_service.py\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"Deprecated and moved to Lib_PY/System/Deprecated/. Project management system being rebuilt from scratch; do not use.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/data/metadata.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"Schema v3.1: added BEJSON_ACRONYM_DEFINITION rule (BOEHNEN ELTON JSON) and PMS_DEPRECATED rule; bumped ECOSYSTEM version to 2.0.42\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/104a.mfdb.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"Manifest v1.33/Schema 2.2.0: bumped Metadata and Library_Changes record_count to reflect this session's additions\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/data/dependencies.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"New entity (Task 1 of MFDB expansion plan): 167 import/require/source edges scanned across Lib_PY, Lib_JS, Lib_TS, Lib_SH\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/104a.mfdb.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"Manifest v1.34/Schema 2.3.0: registered Dependencies entity, record_count 167\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_bejson_chunking.py\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"MFDB-132 self-identification fix: create_mfdb132_package now overwrites Schema_Name->'MFDB-132' and Records_Type->['MFDB-132'] instead of inheriting Chunked-104a identity\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_mfdb_validator.py\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"is_mfdb132_package/validate_mfdb132_package now check for Schema_Name=='MFDB-132' and Records_Type==['MFDB-132'] instead of the old Chunked-104a values\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"TS\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_bejson_chunking.ts\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"MFDB-132 self-identification fix: same Schema_Name/Records_Type overwrite as PY\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"TS\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_mfdb_validators.ts\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"isMfdb132Package/validateMfdb132Package updated to check MFDB-132 identity instead of Chunked-104a\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"SH\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_bejson_chunking.sh\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"MFDB-132 self-identification fix: same Schema_Name/Records_Type overwrite as PY (via jq)\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"SH\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_mfdb_validator.sh\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"mfdb_validator_is_mfdb132_package/validate_mfdb132_package updated to check MFDB-132 identity instead of Chunked-104a\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"JS\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_bejson_chunking.js\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"MFDB-132 self-identification fix: same Schema_Name/Records_Type overwrite as PY\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Core\",\n      \"JS\",\n      \"lib_bejson_Core_mfdb_validator.js\",\n      \"2026-07-21\",\n      \"mfdb_validator_is_mfdb132_package/validate_mfdb132_package updated to check MFDB-132 identity instead of Chunked-104a\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/data/templates.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-22\",\n      \"New entity (Task 2 of MFDB expansion plan): 6 rows - PY/JS-TS/SH file header templates, new-family errors skeleton (PY), MFDB entity skeleton, MFDB manifest skeleton\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/104a.mfdb.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-22\",\n      \"Manifest v1.36/Schema 2.4.0: registered Templates entity, record_count 6\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/data/schemas.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-22\",\n      \"New entity (Task 3 of MFDB expansion plan): 9 rows inventorying every SCHEMA_* constant found across Lib_PY. Resolved SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY_v5/SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY as a true duplicate (byte-identical fields, diffed) - merged to one row. Resolved SCHEMA_MODEL_REGISTRY as a name collision, not a duplicate (Core=Gemini AI_Model schema, AI=OpenRouterModelRegistry schema, genuinely different fields/Records_Type) - kept as two rows, flagged the shared constant name for a future rename pass.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/104a.mfdb.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-22\",\n      \"Manifest v1.37/Schema 2.5.0: registered Schemas entity, record_count 9\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Utility\",\n      \"2.3.2\",\n      \"Lib_PY/Utility/lib_bejson_Utility_bejson_utility.py\",\n      \"2026-07-22\",\n      \"Library bug fix (exemption invoked): removed byte-identical duplicate SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY - now imports SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY_v5 from lib_bejson_Core_bejson_schema.py under the local alias. Verified: import succeeds, same object identity as Core's schema, bejson_utility_create_mfdb_version() tested end-to-end unchanged. Version 2.3.2 -> 2.3.3. Report: BEJSON/Reports/FIX_SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY_DUPLICATE.md. Merged forward into the pkg7 lineage (this fix was made in a branch that also had different plan-doc edits merged from pkg7).\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"AI\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"lib_bejson_AI_bejson_interactions.py\",\n      \"2026-07-24\",\n      \"New file. Implements the Interactions API (POST /v1beta/interactions) via GeminiInteractionsAPI: create_interaction() raw wrapper, chat() full function-call loop, tool_direct() single-shot SI-injection path \\u2014 1:1 mirrors of the confirmed-working client call chain documented in GEMINI_INTERACTIONS_INCIDENT_REPORT.md. Reuses GeminiKeyRegistry/GeminiModelRegistry from lib_bejson_AI_bejson_gemini.py rather than duplicating registry logic. Includes build_text_attachment/build_image_attachment/build_document_attachment/build_attachment helpers (text->no base64, image/document->base64+mime_type; 'inline_data' is deliberately not used, see Incident 5). Uses AI family error codes E_AI_NO_API_KEYS/E_AI_INTERACTIONS_HTTP_ERROR/E_AI_INTERACTIONS_TIMEOUT. Verified end-to-end: chat() two-round function-call exchange, tool_direct() system-instruction injection, and build_attachment() text-file dispatch all tested and passing before this changelog entry was written.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MFDB\",\n      \"N/A\",\n      \"BEJSON/MFDB/104a.mfdb.bejson\",\n      \"2026-07-24\",\n      \"Manifest v1.38/Schema 2.5.1: registered GeminiModelRegistry entity (Lib_PY/AI/gemini_model_registry.104a.bejson, 12 rows, PK model_id). File existed on disk but was never registered until this entry -- change log had gone stale after the 2026-07-22 Schemas-entity bump and was never updated for this registration. Filed retroactively during the 2026-08-15 registry-drift audit/cleanup pass.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"MD\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"lib_bejson_MD_md_errors.py\",\n      \"2026-08-15\",\n      \"Registry-drift cleanup: renumbered E_MD_* codes 70-79 -> 90-109 range (actual codes now 90-99) to resolve a collision with Core's 70-72 (E_MFDB_CORE_ARCHIVE_ERROR/MOUNT_CONFLICT/CREATE_FAILED). Core is priority per Elton Boehnen, 2026-08-15. Constant names unchanged, only numeric values moved. Version 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0.\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}",
